# A template for the development stack's interpolation file (P1.29). Every value here is a placeholder. Copy it to
# ../unset-dev-env/dev-public.env (unset-dev-env is a folder beside this checkout owned by you, mode 0700, with the file
# at 0600), then set the real values there. No live env file lives in the checkout: postgres builds from the repository
# root, and C26 refuses a build context that holds one (architecture record
# 2026-10-12-p127u-bind-ancestors-and-build-context, Amendments 2 and 3). `npm run dev:up` passes that file as
# --interpolation-env to the preflight and as --env-file to Compose; nothing else reads it, and no service gets it
# whole. Secrets never go here: they are files in ../unset-dev-secrets/ (docs/human/runbooks/dev-stack-secrets.md).

# The web server's own origins (interfaces/http/config.ts): the media origin is another site than the public one, and
# both use a TLD in shared/http/config.ts KNOWN_TLDS, so a local stack uses .test names, not .localhost.
WEB_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://app.example.test
WEB_ALLOWED_HOSTS=app.example.test
WEB_MEDIA_ORIGIN=https://media.example.net
